  "narrative": {
    "intro": "American Systems obligated $227M in FY2026 to date. American Systems received 78 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.9M and obligations down 15.0% year over year. Department of Defense obligated $203M, making the Department of Defense the dominant buyer for American Systems; Department of Homeland Security obligated $20.5M and General Services Administration obligated $2.1M. Engineering Services accounted for $79.8M of obligations, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounted for $78M. Custom Computer Programming Services contributed $22.6M and Computer Systems Design Services contributed $20.5M. Other Computer Related Services and Computer Facilities Management Services added $12.9M and $11.5M respectively. Smaller markets include All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $1.3M and Hardware Manufacturing at $244K. Historical annual obligations show FY21 at $228M, FY22 at $220M, FY23 at $288M, FY24 at $295M, and FY25 at $267M, illustrating multi-year variability in obligations without implying a trend beyond the listed figures.",
    "sections": [
